    "title": "<p>Useful histopathological features in the differential diagnosis between inflamed juvenile conjunctival naevus and conjunctival melanoma</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Patricia Chevez-Barrios",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 139.7pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"186\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong>Inflamed juvenile conjunctival naevus</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong>Conjunctival melanoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 139.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"186\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Epithelial junctional naevus component extends beyond stromal component</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Usually absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 139.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"186\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Confluent growth pattern at the epithelial/subepithelial junction</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 139.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"186\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Disorganized naevus nests</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 139.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"186\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Melanocytic maturation in the subepithelial component</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Present</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">May have paradoxical (reverse) maturation, mimicking a lack of maturation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 139.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"186\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Ulceration</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 139.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"186\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Necrosis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">May be present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 139.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"186\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Subepithelial cysts and epithelial nests</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 139.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"186\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Mitoses</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Rare</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Frequent and atypical</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 139.7pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"186\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Inflammatory component</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Present, predominantly at base of naevus (lymphocytes, plasma cells, eosinophils)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Eosinophils in epithelium</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"219\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Absent or scattered (lymphocytes, rarely plasma cells) or brisk between tumour cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  }
]